<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eastern Turkic Khaganate</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Eastern Khaganate</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Eastern Turkic Khaganate was the eastern half of the Gokturk realm after it split into eastern and western branches in the late sixth century. Based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>, it was a major power on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s northern frontier until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a> under Emperor Taizong defeated it in 630, although it was later revived as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-turkic-khaganate">Second Turkic Khaganate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eastern-turkic-khaganate.jpg" alt="Eastern Turkic Khaganate" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photographer: Arzu Emel ALTINKILIÇ · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shoroon_Bumbagar_tomb_mural,_7th_century_CE,_Mongolia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
